1
00:03:25,263 --> 00:03:31,263
Thief. Warrior. Gladiator. King.

2
00:06:50,526 --> 00:06:56,526
Conan the Barbarian is a adventure, fantasy,
action film directed by John Milius.

3
00:10:15,789 --> 00:10:21,789
A horde of rampaging warriors massacre the parents of young Conan and
enslave the young child for years on The Wheel of Pain.

4
00:13:41,052 --> 00:13:47,052
As the sole survivor of the childhood massacre, Conan is released
from slavery and taught the ancient arts of fighting.

5
00:17:06,315 --> 00:17:12,315
Transforming himself into a killing machine, Conan travels into the wilderness to seek
vengeance on Thulsa Doom, the man responsible for killing his family.

6
00:20:31,578 --> 00:20:37,578
In the wilderness, Conan takes up with the thieves Valeria and Subotai.

7
00:23:56,842 --> 00:24:02,842
The group comes upon King Osric, who wants the trio of warriors to help
rescue his daughter who has joined Doom in the hills.

8
00:27:22,105 --> 00:27:28,105
Conan, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

9
00:30:47,368 --> 00:30:53,368
Thulsa Doom, played by James Earl Jones.

10
00:34:12,631 --> 00:34:18,631
King Osric, played by Max von Sydow.

11
00:37:37,894 --> 00:37:43,894
Valeria, played by Sandahl Bergman.

12
00:41:03,157 --> 00:41:09,157
Rexor, played by Ben Davidson.

13
00:44:28,421 --> 00:44:34,421
The Witch, played by Cassandra Gava.

14
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:59,684
Conan the Barbarian is a 1982 American sword-and-sorcery film directed by
John Milius from a screenplay he co-wrote with Oliver Stone.

15
00:51:18,947 --> 00:51:24,947
Based on Robert E.

16
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:50,210
Howard's Conan, the epic film stars Arnold Schwarzenegger and James Earl Jones, and tells the story of a barbarian warrior named Conan
(Schwarzenegger) who seeks to avenge his parents' deaths at the hands of Thulsa Doom (Jones), the leader of a snake cult.

17
00:58:09,473 --> 00:58:15,473
Ideas for a Conan film were proposed as early as
1970; executive producer Edward R.

18
01:01:34,736 --> 01:01:40,736
Pressman and associate producer Edward Summer began a
concerted effort to get the film made in 1975.

19
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It took them two years to obtain the film rights, after which they recruited
Schwarzenegger for the lead role and Stone to draft a script.

20
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
Pressman lacked capital for the endeavor.

21
01:11:50,526 --> 01:11:56,526
In 1979, after having his proposals for investments rejected by the major studios, he sold
the project to Dino De Laurentiis; his daughter Raffaella produced the film.

22
01:15:15,789 --> 01:15:21,789
Milius was appointed as director and he rewrote Stone's script.

23
01:18:41,052 --> 01:18:47,052
The final screenplay integrated elements from various Howard stories, as well
as the Japanese films Seven Samurai (1954) and Kwaidan (1965).

24
01:22:06,315 --> 01:22:12,315
Filming took place in Spain over five months in the regions
around Madrid and the province of Almería.

25
01:25:31,578 --> 01:25:37,578
The sets, designed by Ron Cobb, were based on Dark Age
cultures and Frank Frazetta's paintings of Conan.

26
01:28:56,842 --> 01:29:02,842
Milius eschewed optical effects, preferring to realize his ideas
with mechanical constructs and optical illusions.

27
01:32:22,105 --> 01:32:28,105
Schwarzenegger performed most of his own stunts, and two types of
sword, costing $10,000 each, were forged for his character.

28
01:35:47,368 --> 01:35:53,368
The editing process took over a year, and several violent scenes were cut out.

29
01:39:12,631 --> 01:39:18,631
Conan the Barbarian was distributed by Universal Pictures in the United
States and Canada and 20th Century-Fox in other territories.

30
01:42:37,894 --> 01:42:43,894
It premiered on March 16, 1982, in Spain and May 14, 1982, in North America.

31
01:46:03,157 --> 01:46:09,157
Upon release, the film received mixed reviews from critics and audiences alike, mainly positive for its action sequences, production design, directing,
visual style, and effects, but negatively received for its violent content and screenwriting, as well as some substandard performances.

32
01:49:28,421 --> 01:49:34,421
Despite this, the film became a commercial success for its backers, grossing between $69 million
and $79 million at box offices around the world against its budget of $20 million.

33
01:52:53,684 --> 01:52:59,684
The film earned Schwarzenegger worldwide recognition.

34
01:56:18,947 --> 01:56:24,947
Conan the Barbarian has been frequently released on home video, the sales of which
had increased the film's gross to more than $300 million by 2007.

35
01:59:44,210 --> 01:59:50,210
In the years following its release, it became a cult film, and its
success spawned a sequel, titled Conan the Destroyer (1984).

36
02:03:09,473 --> 02:03:15,473
It ultimately led to the production of a 2011 reboot of the same name.

37
02:06:34,736 --> 02:06:40,736
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
gladiator, fight, magic, repayment.
